 The only hyperparameter we tune per instance is the population size $N_{pop}$. The sensitivity analysis of Section \ref{subsec:sensitivity} showed that $N_{pop}$ is the single hyperparameter with a clear, monotone, scale-dependent effect; the others (generations, crossover rate, mutation rate, evaluation budget) lie on a flat region. Accordingly, for every instance, we select $N_{pop}$ by an adaptive bracket-and-bisect line search with a total budget of five candidate values per algorithm.
 
